# 1) Define a CI-friendly summary contract

You already have `matrix-summary.json`. That’s great for humans, but CI benefits from a smaller stable shape.

## `src/eval/regressionTypes.ts`

```ts
export type CombinationRegressionSummary = {
  promptVersion: string;
  model: string;
  successRate: number;
  avgHeuristicScore: number;
  heuristicStdDev: number;
  stabilityLabel: "high" | "medium" | "low";
  avgDurationMs: number;
  estimatedAvgCostPerRunUsd: number;
  caseWinCount: number;
  tiedCaseCount: number;
  strictValidationPassCount: number;
  normalizationUsedCount: number;
  topFailedCheckIds: Array<{
    id: string;
    count: number;
  }>;
};

export type EvalRegressionSnapshot = {
  createdAt: string;
  runCount: number;
  totalCases: number;
  combinations: CombinationRegressionSummary[];
};
```

This is the “contract” your CI comparison should use.

